  "interpretation": "Consistent joint point-estimate improvement on reused development audit.",
  "limitations": [
    "Already-observed development audit; no independent confirmation and no new official-test score.",
    "PCA anisotropy is a nonlinear re-expression of existing covariance. The five line-strip features add spatial arrangement descriptors, but the block ablation cannot isolate each feature contribution.",
    "Three seeds share the same wafers; their averages and spread do not increase sample size.",
    "Strip width and direction grid were fixed before scores; the descriptor is a coarse heuristic, can respond to chance alignments, and can miss curved or discontinuous scratches.",
    "Error-feature associations and gallery impressions are descriptive, not causal explanations; original potentially ambiguous labels are retained.",
    "CPU RF prediction times and reused CNN logits are not a matched hardware latency benchmark."
  ],
  "feature_caveat": "71 original features already include full defect covariance. Added six features were evaluated as a single fixed block, not claimed as six independent new signals.",
